- **Quick snap** button appears in the share sheet above the file picker (only when the page is HTTPS/localhost and the browser has a camera).
- **Tap the shutter → photo**, captured from the live video frame to a JPEG.
- **Hold the shutter (~320 ms) → video**; a progress bar and `0:07 · 13s left` countdown run while recording, releasing stops it, and it **stops itself at 20 seconds** so the existing `MAX_VIDEO_SECONDS` limit can't be exceeded.
- **Presets** — the same six filters (Original/HD/90s Vintage/Retro/Sepia/Classic) apply live to the preview via CSS. They're stored as `filter_name` metadata, exactly like uploads, so nothing is baked into the pixels and the gallery renders them the same way.
- **Front/back switch**, captured photos mirrored when using the selfie camera so the result matches the preview; multiple snaps per session with a thumbnail strip; **Done (n)** hands the files back to the upload sheet.
- Failures are explicit: permission denied, no camera, or a browser without `MediaRecorder` all show a plain message with a "Choose from device instead" escape hatch.

## Files

- [CameraCapture.jsx](src/components/wedding/CameraCapture.jsx) — the overlay, capture, recording and preset UI.
- [UploadModal.jsx](src/components/wedding/UploadModal.jsx) — the Quick snap entry point, passing remaining allowances into the camera and merging captured files into the pending list.
- [FilterPicker.jsx](src/components/wedding/FilterPicker.jsx) — now controlled by its `value`; it previously kept a private copy, so a preset chosen in the camera wouldn't have highlighted back in the sheet.
- [README.md](README.md) — documented the new flow.

Container selection is defensive: the recorder skips codec strings that name an audio codec when the stream has no audio track, and falls back across MP4 → WebM → browser default. Without that, a mic-denied stream throws `NotSupportedError` and recording silently dies.

## Verified in the browser

I stubbed `getUserMedia` with a canvas stream (no physical camera here) and drove the real UI:

- Shutter tap → `snap-20261030-160833.jpg`, thumbnail appeared, Done counter incremented.
- 1.3 s hold → header switched to `0:01 · 19s left`, label to "Release to stop recording", release produced `clip-20261030-160835.mp4`.
- Presets applied live: Sepia → `sepia(0.75) contrast(0.95)`, Classic → `grayscale(1) contrast(1.12) brightness(0.97)`, HD → `saturate(1.12)…`; the chosen preset was still selected in the upload sheet afterwards.
- Held past the limit: progress reached 75% at 15 s, then at 20 s recording stopped **without releasing**, the clip was kept, and the shutter reverted to idle.
- Pending files merged into the sheet; Cancel left the gallery untouched (still 0 moments).
- Ended stream (from reusing one fake stream) produced the graceful "Recording video is not supported" path rather than a crash.
- `npm run build` passes.

Two honest gaps: the real camera and microphone on a phone weren't exercised — only a synthetic stream — and I deliberately didn't tap Share, so these captured files haven't been through a real Cloudinary upload. Also worth knowing: iOS Safari's `MediaRecorder` produces MP4 only on reasonably recent versions; older iPhones will fall to the "not supported" message, and the file picker still works there.
