## How it works

In the full-screen preview in [UploadModal.jsx](src/components/wedding/UploadModal.jsx):

- **Pointer-based gestures** (`pointerdown/move/up`), so touch, stylus and mouse drag all behave identically — no separate touch-only code path to rot.
- **The image follows the finger**: the card translates live with your drag (`translateX`), with a 180 ms ease back into place if you don't commit.
- **Threshold**: a swipe must travel more than the smaller of 110 px or 16% of the screen width, so it feels deliberate on both a 390 px iPhone and a tablet. Below that it snaps back and nothing changes.
- **Direction lock**: the first ~10 px decides. If the gesture is more vertical than horizontal it's abandoned immediately, so page scrolling and other vertical movement are never hijacked — reinforced with `touch-action: pan-y` on the stage.
- **Wrap-around**: swiping left on the last item returns to the first, and vice versa, matching the arrows.
- **"Swipe to browse"** appears under the counter whenever there's more than one item, so the gesture is discoverable.
- **Single item**: gestures are ignored entirely.
- **Edge case handled**: a short drag that ends outside the preview area (before pointer capture kicks in) resets on pointer-leave rather than leaving the image stuck mid-offset. The `key` on the media wrapper also forces a fresh element per item, so a video doesn't keep playing under the next photo.

## Verified in the browser

Driving real pointer events at the preview:

- Swipe **left** 210 px → `1 / 2` → `2 / 2`.
